---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { repository } from "../../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ScreenRecorder development"
  description="Build requirements and source layout for contributors to the ScreenRecorder project."
>
  <article class="guide wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/docs/">← All documentation</a><div
      class="eyebrow"
    >
      CONTRIBUTE · 3 MIN READ
    </div><h1>
      Built in the open.<br /><span class="accent-word">Join in.</span>
    </h1><p class="guide-lead">
      ScreenRecorder is a native C++20 project with separate Windows and Fedora
      implementations. The static website lives in its own <code>website/</code> directory.
    </p><h2>Windows build</h2><ul class="guide-list">
      <li>Windows 10/11 x64</li><li>
        Visual Studio 2026 / Build Tools 18 with C++ workload
      </li><li>Windows SDK 10.0.26100 or later</li><li>CMake 3.20 or later</li>
    </ul><pre><code>cmake -B build -G "Visual Studio 18 2026" -A x64
cmake --build build --config Debug
ctest --test-dir build -C Debug --output-on-failure</code></pre><h2
    >
      Fedora build
    </h2><p>
      The Fedora app is developed separately in <code>fedora-linux-app/</code>.
      Its README documents the current dependencies, Ninja build, installation,
      and RPM packaging workflow.
    </p><h2>Website development</h2><p>
      The site is Astro and TypeScript, built statically. From the website
      directory:
    </p><pre><code>pnpm install
pnpm dev
pnpm build</code></pre><h2>
      Contributing
    </h2><p>
      Open an issue to discuss larger changes, then submit a focused pull
      request with a clear description. See the project contribution guide and
      CI workflows on GitHub.
    </p><a
      class="text-link guide-next"
      href={`${repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}
      >Read contribution guide ↗</a
    >
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
